Z||000000||BAM-BAM||05-29-2001||09:13 AM||||  I was traveling north on I-15 between Mesquite Nevada and St. George Utah on my way to move my oldest boy home for the summer. I had just started into the Virgin River gorge when a Gold Fiero notchback flew by me. It was beautiful. I couldn't really get a close look at it do to the speed differential, but it did have Colorado plates. Gold notchback with a spoiler, I am thinking it was an 87SE. I'm not sure if they made them in gold in 86 and I know that they were silver in 85. Oh yeah, I almost forgot, aero fascia and ground effects like the Indy's and 85GT's. Let me know who you are. There were two people inside just having way to much fun while I was trapped in my Suburban, lumbering my way through those twisty curves. Damn I was jealous! Well, at least someone was having a ball. It was nice to see a Fiero in action  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||8
